From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adrian Schupp <as@satware.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 20:30:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: google: gs201-cheetah: restore the
 software reboot reason

Stock ships a second reboot-reason writer for the Pixel 7 Pro besides
the syscon-reboot-mode node that gs201.dtsi keeps: Google's
pixel-gs201-reboot.c writes SYSIP_DAT0 and then the RSBM record into
the MAX77759's MAXQ user memory (BMS_RSBM_VALID | reason into
GBMS_TAG_RSBM). Give the Pixel 7 Pro that second writer, the
nvmem-based path the gs101 Pixels carry in gs101-pixel-common.dtsi: an
nvmem-0 cell of the I2C PMIC (max77759-nvmem, fixed layout) and a
root-level nvmem-reboot-mode node.

Only mode-bootloader (0x800000fc) is mapped for now: recovery, fastboot
and charge send ABL into paths nobody has exercised on slot B, and an
unmapped reason writes nothing, which matches stock. The existing
syscon-reboot-mode keeps working in parallel; whether ABL needs the
RSBM write is still being tested.

Signed-off-by: Adrian Schupp <as@satware.com>
Assisted-by: LLM opencode
---
 .../boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-cheetah.dts  | 42 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 42 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-cheetah.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-cheetah.dts
index 7869064b0..8290c2dea 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-cheetah.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-cheetah.dts
@@ -120,6 +120,22 @@ button-power {
 		};
 	};
 
+	/*
+	 * Second reboot-reason writer, the nvmem path stock ships besides
+	 * the syscon-reboot-mode node in gs201.dtsi: Google's
+	 * pixel-gs201-reboot.c writes SYSIP_DAT0 and then the RSBM record
+	 * (BMS_RSBM_VALID | reason) into the MAX77759's MAXQ user memory.
+	 * Same shape as gs101-pixel-common.dtsi; only bootloader is mapped
+	 * until the other modes are proven on slot B. Whether ABL needs the
+	 * RSBM write is still being tested.
+	 */
+	reboot-mode {
+		compatible = "nvmem-reboot-mode";
+		nvmem-cells = <&nvmem_reboot_mode>;
+		nvmem-cell-names = "reboot-mode";
+		mode-bootloader = <0x800000fc>;
+	};
+
 	/*
 	 * UFS VCC. Google drives it from GPIO gpp0-1 (boot-on); there is no
 	 * gs201 GPIO driver yet, so describe it as always on, as the
@@ -677,6 +693,32 @@ gpio {
 			interrupt-controller;
 			#interrupt-cells = <2>;
 		};
+
+		nvmem-0 {
+			compatible = "maxim,max77759-nvmem";
+
+			nvmem-layout {
+				compatible = "fixed-layout";
+				#address-cells = <1>;
+				#size-cells = <1>;
+
+				nvmem_reboot_mode: reboot-mode@0 {
+					reg = <0x0 0x4>;
+				};
+
+				boot-reason@4 {
+					reg = <0x4 0x4>;
+				};
+
+				shutdown-user-flag@8 {
+					reg = <0x8 0x1>;
+				};
+
+				rsoc@a {
+					reg = <0xa 0x2>;
+				};
+			};
+		};
 	};
 };
 
